# What goes into the source distribution beyond what setuptools
# works out for itself.
#
# The wheel gets the bundled datasets through
# `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` in pyproject.toml, and the sdist
# picks those up too because they live inside the package. These
# four do not -- they sit at the repository root, and without this
# they are simply absent from the sdist.
#
# CITATION.cff matters most of the three: this library bundles other
# people's data and implements other people's methods, and the file
# saying how to cite it should travel with the source rather than
# only existing on a web page somebody may not find.

include CITATION.cff
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include REFERENCES.md

# Excluded on purpose: `docs/` builds an API reference from the
# installed package's own docstrings, so shipping the .rst wrappers
# in the sdist would add files that cannot be built from it without
# the whole dev environment anyway.
prune docs
prune examples
prune app
prune tools
prune .github
